+       * statement of the risk; it is accepted because a spin is not a recovery.
        *
-       * It is left as a log line rather than a behaviour change because this is
-       * the hot SMC path that every working session runs through thousands of
-       * times, and RWX faults on one page legitimately repeat -- so a breaker
-       * here would risk a regression to fix a branch that has not yet been
-       * shown to be the one looping. If it is, this line says so once and names
-       * the page, and that is the fact needed to justify touching it.
+       * The invalidation above has already happened and is deliberately not
+       * undone. It costs a recompile and is correct either way.
        *
-       * IFmt would be filtered by 0003's default ERROR ceiling, which is the
